Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 06:24:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Verify Stripe payment before showing checkout success; add
 cart badge and 404 page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- /checkout/success previously showed 'Thank you, your payment has
  been submitted successfully' and cleared the cart to anyone who
  simply visited the URL, paid or not, with no server-side check.
  Added /api/checkout/verify which confirms payment_status === 'paid'
  via the Stripe API before the page claims success or touches the cart.
  Visiting without a valid, paid session now shows an honest
  'we couldn't confirm that order' state and leaves the cart untouched.
- Added components/CartBadge.tsx and wired it into every BAG link
  (home, products, product detail). The elarossa-cart-updated event
  was already being dispatched from three places but nothing was
  listening for it — the cart count was invisible from the nav.
- Added app/not-found.tsx so 404s match the site's design instead of
  falling back to Next's default unstyled page.
